WEBVTT

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:09.625
-What is he doing?
-I have no idea.

00:00:09.708 --> 00:00:12.083
What are those things?

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.208
Glad you could finally join us.

00:00:19.291 --> 00:00:22.958
Shh! Quiet, you guys.
You're gonna give away our position.

00:00:23.041 --> 00:00:26.333
My patience wanes.
Why haven't you found it yet?

00:00:27.541 --> 00:00:32.916
-Ooh, pretty! Whoa.
-You fool!

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:35.375
You know how fragile and powerful
these are!

00:00:35.458 --> 00:00:38.833
Just a few more
and I will finally have enough

00:00:38.916 --> 00:00:41.625
to take over the Dream World!

00:00:41.708 --> 00:00:46.791
Well, that isn't good. And why
does he sound and look so creepy?

00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:48.250
Should we call the others?

00:00:48.333 --> 00:00:50.291
Let's figure out
what that thing is first.

00:00:50.375 --> 00:00:53.750
Would be easier
if we still had our hourglasses.

00:00:53.833 --> 00:00:55.750
It doesn't matter if it's harder now.

00:00:55.833 --> 00:00:58.416
And if that thing is as powerful
as the Nightmare King says,

00:00:58.500 --> 00:01:00.333
then we need to get it away from him.

00:01:00.416 --> 00:01:02.916
-How?
-Oh! Sigma-two-glide-swipe.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.750
Classic. Let's do it.

00:01:06.750 --> 00:01:10.458
Hey! Why did the Nightmare King
cross the road?

00:01:10.541 --> 00:01:11.875
You!

00:01:11.958 --> 00:01:14.625
-Why did you cross the road?
-Fool!

00:01:14.708 --> 00:01:16.958
This is not a riddle or a joke!

00:01:17.041 --> 00:01:20.375
It is a diversion
clearly meant to distract us.

00:01:20.458 --> 00:01:23.041
It's a common strategy
an enemy will resort to

00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:25.250
when they realize they're outnumbered
and underpowered.

00:01:25.333 --> 00:01:26.166
Yes.

00:01:26.250 --> 00:01:28.541
It is meant to stall escalation

00:01:28.625 --> 00:01:31.958
and provide the weaker party
more time to mount countermeasures

00:01:32.041 --> 00:01:33.500
and thus grow an advantage.

00:01:33.583 --> 00:01:38.166
And get you to monologue long enough
for us to do what we needed to do!

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:40.083
What?

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:41.833
Outfoxed you!

00:01:41.916 --> 00:01:43.750
Get me back my crystal!

00:01:43.833 --> 00:01:46.166
Keep going, Iz! We'll cover you!

00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:50.208
With or without an hourglass,
we can do this! Ready, Z?

00:01:50.291 --> 00:01:52.583
This will be epic!

00:01:55.333 --> 00:01:56.875
Or not.

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:05.333
-Mateo!
-Get it out of here!

00:02:05.416 --> 00:02:08.208
Call the others!

00:02:08.291 --> 00:02:10.791
I gotta call in reinforcements and--
Whoa!

00:02:15.791 --> 00:02:21.208
Oh, my gosh, you are so cute!

00:02:27.583 --> 00:02:30.458
Save my brother! Go!

00:02:34.583 --> 00:02:37.791
Come here! You're mine!

00:02:57.208 --> 00:02:59.833
This is more like it!

00:03:01.708 --> 00:03:04.250
Awesome!

00:03:37.625 --> 00:03:42.125
We will meet again, Dream Chaser!

00:03:42.208 --> 00:03:46.625
I still don't get it!
Why did you cross the road?

00:03:51.458 --> 00:03:52.750
So cute!

00:03:52.833 --> 00:03:54.875
Let's call the others
and tell them what's going on.

00:03:54.958 --> 00:03:57.291
I would, but mistakes were made.

00:03:57.375 --> 00:03:59.791
Then we'll find them ourselves.
Come on!

